1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:02,480
Hand me that flashlight."

2
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:04,940
(Sheldon:)Those were the last words

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,740
(Sheldon:)he ever spoke to us.

4
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:08,120
(Leonard:)I don't think you need

5
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:11,130
(Leonard:)to worry about death by badgers
being hereditary.

6
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:12,590
(Sheldon:)Not true.

7
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:15,300
(Sheldon:)The fight or flight instinct
is coded genetically.

8
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:19,320
(Sheldon:)Instead of fleeing, he chose
to fight barehanded

9
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:21,970
(Sheldon:)against a brawny member
of the weasel family.

10
00:00:21,970 --> 00:00:25,220
(Sheldon:)Who's to say that I don't share
that flawed DNA?

11
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:27,790
(Leonard:)You can always get a badger
and find out.

12
00:00:31,650 --> 00:00:33,400
(Sheldon:)But seriously,

13
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,070
(Sheldon:)even if I disregard
the Uncle Carl factor,

14
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:38,520
(Sheldon:)at best I have 60 years left.

15
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:41,120
(Leonard:)That long, huh?

16
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,770
(Sheldon:)60 only takes me to here.

17
00:00:42,770 --> 00:00:44,980
(Sheldon:)I need to get to here.

18
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:46,830
(Leonard:)What's there?

19
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:49,610
(Sheldon:)The earliest estimate
of the singularity,

20
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:51,830
(Sheldon:)when man will be able
to transfer his consciousness

21
00:00:51,830 --> 00:00:54,550
(Sheldon:)into machines
and achieve immortality.

22
00:00:54,550 --> 00:00:57,970
(Leonard:)So, you're upset
about missing out

23
00:00:57,970 --> 00:01:00,690
(Leonard:)on becoming some sort of
freakish self-aware robot?

